WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:02.750
- Of course all parents say
that they love you all equally.

00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:04.330
They treat all their children the same.

00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:07.323
But all middle children
know, we are forgotten about.

00:00:07.323 --> 00:00:09.900
(laughs) My mom's gonna kill me for this.

00:00:11.316 --> 00:00:14.321
(soft playful music)

00:00:14.321 --> 00:00:19.321
(whooshing)
(creaking)

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:21.670
- I am the second child of four.

00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:24.020
At one point, I was the
second child of three,

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:27.490
and then my youngest sister
surprised us (laughs).

00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:28.323
Or blessed us.

00:00:28.323 --> 00:00:30.590
- I am the middle child, one of five.

00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:32.330
I guess here that's considered pretty big.

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:34.700
My parents are, both originally
were born in Nigeria,

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:36.340
so they had bigger families.

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:38.390
- I'm technically a middle child.

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:40.820
My dad had a son from a previous marriage,

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:42.310
and then when he got with my mom,

00:00:42.310 --> 00:00:43.680
then she had my younger sister.

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:46.550
- I have an older brother
and a younger sister.

00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:50.570
I am very much like Stephanie
from Full House, I'd say.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:52.776
- Thank you, Stephanie.

00:00:52.776 --> 00:00:54.240
(organ playing)

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:55.399
Thank you, Stephanie.

00:00:55.399 --> 00:00:57.039
(audience laughing)

00:00:57.039 --> 00:00:57.872
Thanks, Steph.

00:00:57.872 --> 00:01:00.160
- I definitely got plenty of
attention from my parents,

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:02.150
but when I was a kid it
never felt like enough.

00:01:02.150 --> 00:01:05.050
- When it came to mines and
my parents' relationship,

00:01:05.050 --> 00:01:07.820
they sort of like knew
that I would be okay.

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:10.170
- It was always, oh take care of the baby,

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:12.630
or oh it's the oldest, you
have all this responsibility

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:13.860
that you're supposed to do.

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:16.410
And then the middle child just
kind of floats in between.

00:01:16.410 --> 00:01:19.550
There was one time I went
to my sixth grade dance.

00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:21.580
My parents said that they
were gonna come pick me up,

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:24.050
and I was the last kid
outside just sitting like.

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:27.250
(crickets chirping)

00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:28.990
Nobodies here to get me.

00:01:28.990 --> 00:01:31.730
I had no phone to call anybody.

00:01:31.730 --> 00:01:33.370
It traumatized me so much.

00:01:33.370 --> 00:01:34.970
Would they have done that
to my younger sister?

00:01:34.970 --> 00:01:35.810
Absolutely not.

00:01:35.810 --> 00:01:37.490
They would have been there at five o'clock

00:01:37.490 --> 00:01:38.323
when the dance ended.

00:01:38.323 --> 00:01:41.120
- There are a lot of home movies of me

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:43.830
trying to get as much screen
time as I possibly could.

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:45.750
You can definitely tell
when my sister was born,

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:48.610
because once my dad started
filming her instead of me,

00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:50.500
I would throw myself
in front of the camera

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:51.940
every time he was filming her.

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:55.780
- When the middle child
tells you something,

00:01:55.780 --> 00:01:58.230
believe them because for the most part,

00:01:58.230 --> 00:02:00.100
there's a lot of things
that the middle child

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:00.933
is just trying to get across.

00:02:00.933 --> 00:02:02.780
Like, "look see this."

00:02:02.780 --> 00:02:04.490
And a lot of people don't pay attention.

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:05.538
I think in between my siblings,

00:02:05.538 --> 00:02:07.700
I was always the weird one.

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:10.370
They would get along with
each other, really fine.

00:02:10.370 --> 00:02:12.520
I always went to sleep
early so they would stay up

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:14.310
watching movies and playing video games.

00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:16.560
I sort of ended up being
like the third wheel.

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:19.390
- I wanted the respect of my siblings.

00:02:19.390 --> 00:02:22.990
Even to this day, that is
something I want more of.

00:02:22.990 --> 00:02:25.310
Growing up when I was younger,

00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:27.729
they did not look to me at all (laughs).

00:02:27.729 --> 00:02:29.090
It's always the curse of the middle child.

00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:31.740
- My older brother and my
younger sister are pretty close.

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:33.970
They tease me a lot
about how organized I am,

00:02:33.970 --> 00:02:36.250
and how clean I am, how
I'm always nagging at them

00:02:36.250 --> 00:02:37.760
to clean up after themselves,

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:40.000
but they always know
that they won't do it,

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:42.490
and so then I will so they
kind of abuse it a little bit.

00:02:42.490 --> 00:02:43.960
They get me to do stuff
that they don't wanna do.

00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:46.150
I've always kind of felt like sometimes

00:02:46.150 --> 00:02:48.090
they do kind of pick on me.

00:02:48.090 --> 00:02:51.480
- When my brother came around,
we would just bump heads.

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:52.686
- You didn't tell
everybody about the years

00:02:52.686 --> 00:02:54.040
of torment that I put you through.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:56.128
- I never got to see you very often.

00:02:56.128 --> 00:02:56.961
- Right.

00:02:56.961 --> 00:02:59.720
- And so I would always be
this close to you (laughs).

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:00.813
- [Michael] And when we got together.

00:03:00.813 --> 00:03:01.646
- [Destinee] Yeah.

00:03:01.646 --> 00:03:02.808
- [Michael] Because of that.

00:03:02.808 --> 00:03:04.099
(Destinee laughs)

00:03:04.099 --> 00:03:05.766
- Come on, let's go!

00:03:06.772 --> 00:03:08.980
No, Michael, come on, I'm serious!

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:11.460
I remember one time you tried
to push me down the stairs.

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:12.440
- I won't deny that.

00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:14.230
I also won't agree that that's true.

00:03:14.230 --> 00:03:17.810
- Michael and my younger
sister, Raven, got along fine.

00:03:17.810 --> 00:03:19.620
I'm over here fighting
for Michael's attention,

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:21.170
and Michael's over here
fighting for Raven's.

00:03:21.170 --> 00:03:23.340
- On behalf of middle children everywhere,

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:26.000
I would say to older and younger siblings,

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:28.730
just ease up on the middle
children a little bit.

00:03:28.730 --> 00:03:29.970
We're very sensitive.

00:03:29.970 --> 00:03:32.500
We just want to love you,
we just want you to love us.

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:34.570
- My biggest advice for
any middle child out there,

00:03:34.570 --> 00:03:36.430
find a creative way to get attention.

00:03:36.430 --> 00:03:38.660
My coping mechanism for
trying to get attention

00:03:38.660 --> 00:03:41.270
was being as good at
possible at athletics.

00:03:41.270 --> 00:03:43.960
So, I literally played every sport

00:03:43.960 --> 00:03:45.560
my high school had to offer.

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:48.640
I was on the soccer team,
volleyball team, basketball team,

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:50.820
I ran track, and I made
sure my parents were

00:03:50.820 --> 00:03:52.750
at every possible event,
because I was like,

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:53.670
"You are gonna watch me,

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:55.160
and you are gonna watch me be great."

00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:56.440
- To get my parents' attention,

00:03:56.440 --> 00:03:59.910
I took on acting and singing
and things like that.

00:03:59.910 --> 00:04:01.470
I did a lot of school plays,

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:03.900
so inevitably my parents
would have to come to them

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:05.500
and watch me perform and I would

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:06.530
get all the attention that day.

00:04:06.530 --> 00:04:08.160
- In school, I was a really good student.

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:10.340
Since you aren't given
the opportunity to just

00:04:10.340 --> 00:04:12.327
be your own person, then
you start doing things

00:04:12.327 --> 00:04:13.830
that are very unique.

00:04:13.830 --> 00:04:15.050
You want to make a statement.

00:04:15.050 --> 00:04:16.430
- Middle children are trendsetters.

00:04:16.430 --> 00:04:18.080
They're the pioneers, they're
the ones that are going

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:19.700
to go out and make something happen,

00:04:19.700 --> 00:04:20.830
even when it's never been done.

00:04:20.830 --> 00:04:22.610
Middle children are a handful,

00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:24.400
but they're going to be
one of your biggest gifts,

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:25.730
and you're gonna get the most out of them.

00:04:25.730 --> 00:04:27.810
- I feel like being a middle
child comes with its perks

00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:29.599
because no body's paying attention to you,

00:04:29.599 --> 00:04:32.660
you kind of get to do some
things under the radar.

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:35.070
- I didn't have to be the
first to do everything,

00:04:35.070 --> 00:04:36.810
and my parents were able to get out

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:39.910
all of their first-parent
stuff with my brother.

00:04:39.910 --> 00:04:42.120
When it came to me, they were
a little bit more lenient

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:43.410
and a little bit more loose.

00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:45.580
- Being the middle child,
there was pressure to follow

00:04:45.580 --> 00:04:48.400
the footsteps of my brothers
and sisters in front of me.

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:50.810
And I did not adhere to that.

00:04:50.810 --> 00:04:54.680
I think figured out sooner than
later that this was my life

00:04:54.680 --> 00:04:56.980
and, especially for my
culture, my background,

00:04:56.980 --> 00:05:00.570
being Nigerian, that
was not the script that

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:01.403
I was supposed to follow.

00:05:01.403 --> 00:05:03.720
My parents were really
really big on education.

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:06.200
When it came to college, I was like,

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:08.410
I'll do it, but then when
I was there I was like,

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:10.950
I want something more, so I left.

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:14.900
And that was the biggest
shock to hit my family ever.

00:05:14.900 --> 00:05:17.700
I was the first and only child to this day

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:20.480
to ever to make the decision
to walk away from college.

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:24.520
Being the middle child, I
had the opportunity to be me.

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:26.100
And I think when you're older,

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:27.860
you don't have that opportunity, I think

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:31.420
you have an expectation to
represent the family first.

00:05:31.420 --> 00:05:34.340
- As the middle child,
you're given a lot of space

00:05:34.340 --> 00:05:38.370
to sort of create your own
identity away from your family.

00:05:38.370 --> 00:05:42.380
Because my family is
really traditional Mexican,

00:05:42.380 --> 00:05:44.950
there was a lot of things that I sort of

00:05:44.950 --> 00:05:46.960
broke the rules in.

00:05:46.960 --> 00:05:49.590
I was the first child to move out at 18

00:05:49.590 --> 00:05:51.890
because I was the first
child to go to college.

00:05:51.890 --> 00:05:53.900
Being a vegetarian, that's something

00:05:53.900 --> 00:05:56.220
unheard of in a Mexican-American family.

00:05:56.220 --> 00:05:58.540
When I was vegetarian, I went to Mexico.

00:05:58.540 --> 00:06:00.900
Everywhere you go in my
parents' little town,

00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:01.880
there's street tacos.

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:04.050
I really wanted tacos,
but I was a vegetarian,

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:06.580
so what I did was that I had tacos

00:06:06.580 --> 00:06:10.450
made of lettuce and carrots and that is

00:06:10.450 --> 00:06:11.290
an ongoing joke.

00:06:11.290 --> 00:06:13.330
My family still jokes about that today.

00:06:13.330 --> 00:06:15.890
- As a middle child, I
definitely felt like the mediator

00:06:15.890 --> 00:06:17.440
within my entire family.

00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:19.490
- I definitely think I
bring the family together.

00:06:19.490 --> 00:06:20.800
Onyi's going to provide a good time.

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:23.800
He's either gonna end up
DJing the party for us,

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:25.610
he's gonna end up mixing drinks for us,

00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:27.020
he's gonna make sure we're laughing,

00:06:27.020 --> 00:06:28.390
we're joking, we're having fun.

00:06:28.390 --> 00:06:31.350
- On family trips, I kind of
had to balance everyone out

00:06:31.350 --> 00:06:33.180
and make sure everyone
was having a good time.

00:06:33.180 --> 00:06:35.340
And I think that's a role
that the middle child

00:06:35.340 --> 00:06:36.490
usually takes on?

00:06:36.490 --> 00:06:37.600
I wouldn't change it for the world.

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:39.090
- One thing that people don't really know

00:06:39.090 --> 00:06:40.290
about middle children is,

00:06:40.290 --> 00:06:42.270
if you really need them
and you tell them that,

00:06:42.270 --> 00:06:43.103
they'll be there for you.

00:06:43.103 --> 00:06:44.050
They will not let you down.

00:06:44.050 --> 00:06:45.190
- I feel like that we're older

00:06:45.190 --> 00:06:46.790
and that we're all adults, the three of us

00:06:46.790 --> 00:06:48.190
are all on the same playing field.

00:06:48.190 --> 00:06:50.520
When we get together,
we're just goofy as fuck.

00:06:50.520 --> 00:06:51.610
We don't make sense.

00:06:51.610 --> 00:06:53.080
- We're all pretty close now.

00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:55.236
We like to play board
games and things like that.

00:06:55.236 --> 00:06:56.270
- Even though there were five of us,

00:06:56.270 --> 00:06:57.860
it always felt like love.

00:06:57.860 --> 00:06:59.164
They were my homies, my best friends.

00:06:59.164 --> 00:07:01.600
Because we knew our
parents were working hard

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:02.830
just to provide for us,

00:07:02.830 --> 00:07:05.354
so we always had each
other, and that was enough.

00:07:05.354 --> 00:07:10.271
(whistling)
(upbeat music)

